# Base edge config for the shared `core` Caddy service.
#
# This file declares NO sites of its own. Each active profile's site blocks are
# imported from fragments that the deploy places into /etc/caddy/conf.d/ for the
# currently active COMPOSE_PROFILES (e.g. product/caddy/product.caddy,
# observability/caddy/grafana.caddy). So the served sites always track what is
# actually deployed. A zero-match glob is a harmless warning, not an error.

# Which upstream proxies may speak for the client. Defaults to a documentation
# CIDR (RFC 5737) that no real peer ever matches, so out of the box Caddy is
# the direct internet edge and ignores any inbound X-Forwarded-For. Set
# TRUSTED_PROXIES in .env only when a load balancer or CDN really is in front;
# that is what makes `client_ip` below resolve to the true client address.
{
	servers {
		trusted_proxies static {$TRUSTED_PROXIES}
	}
}

# Reusable access guard for internal / operator-only vhosts (*.$INTERNAL_DOMAIN).
# Any internal fragment invokes it with `import internal_guard`; the allowlist is
# INTERNAL_ALLOW_IPS in .env (space-separated CIDRs, v4 and/or v6). Non-matching
# source IPs get 403 before reaching the upstream. `client_ip` is the client
# address after TRUSTED_PROXIES is applied — identical to the socket peer when
# nothing is in front, and still correct when something is.
(internal_guard) {
	@external not client_ip {$INTERNAL_ALLOW_IPS}
	respond @external "Forbidden" 403
}

import /etc/caddy/conf.d/*.caddy
